<?xml version="1.0"?>

<launch>

    <arg name="launch_only_arm" default="false" />

        <let name="urdf_path" 
            value="$(find-pkg-share my_robot_description)/urdf/standalone_arm.urdf.xacro"
            if="$(var launch_only_arm)" />
        <let name="urdf_path" 
            value="$(find-pkg-share my_robot_description)/urdf/my_robot.urdf.xacro"
            unless="$(var launch_only_arm)" />   
        <let name="gazebo_config_path" 
            value="$(find-pkg-share my_robot_bringup)/config/gazebo_bridge.yaml" />
        <let name="rviz_config_path" 
            value="$(find-pkg-share my_robot_description)/rviz/arm_config.rviz"
            if="$(var launch_only_arm)" />
        <let name="rviz_config_path" 
            value="$(find-pkg-share my_robot_description)/rviz/urdf_config_far_view.rviz"
            unless="$(var launch_only_arm)" />
        <let name="world_path"
            value="$(find-pkg-share my_robot_bringup)/worlds/test_world.sdf" />

    <node pkg="robot_state_publisher" exec="robot_state_publisher">
        <param name="robot_description" type="str" value="$(command 'xacro $(var urdf_path)')" />
    </node>
    
    <!-- A launch file is included, while a runnable executable node is started with the <node> tag -->
    <include file="$(find-pkg-share ros_gz_sim)/launch/gz_sim.launch.py" >
        <arg name="gz_args" value="$(var world_path) -r" />

        <!-- We don't need to have $(command '') because this is an arg, that other one was a param -->   
        <!-- <arg name="gz_args" value="empty.sdf -r" /> -->
    </include>

    <node pkg="ros_gz_sim" exec="create" args="-topic robot_description" />

    <node pkg="ros_gz_bridge" exec="parameter_bridge">
        <param name="config_file" value="$(var gazebo_config_path)" />
    </node>

    <node pkg="rviz2" exec="rviz2" output="screen"
          args="-d $(var rviz_config_path)" />

</launch>

<!--
  NOTES

    The package ros_gz_sim is provided through "source /opt/ros/jazzy"

    In <param name="" value="" type="" >
    no type=    → "ROS, figure out what type this value is and load it to name parameter"
    type="str"  → "ROS, this IS a string; don't try to figure it out"

    ROS's own release documentation explicitly recommends type="str" when a launch parameter needs to be interpreted as a string.

    Gazebo and ROS are unrelated, they cannot see eachother's topics for example. We need a so-called "bridge".

    ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard let's you control the robot with keystrokes

    We need to publish joint states, on display.launch.xml we used <node pkg="joint_state_publisher_gui" exec="joint_state_publisher_gui" />
    which was provided to us from /opt/ros/jazzy. Here, we use the plugin <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-state-publisher-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointStatePublisher">

    The <arg name="launch_only_arm" default="0" /> makes if-else logic, here if-unless
    AND it makes so it can be changed at launch from the terminal by writing
    ros2 launch my_robot_bringup my_robot_gazebo.launch.xml launch_only_arm:=true (or false)

    ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames -o <file_name> generates pdf of the frame tree
    
-->